\pard\sb320\sa160\cf2\b\fs30 4. Preprocessing\par

\pard\sa160\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\fs22 Several features in the raw dataset (Glucose, BloodPressure, SkinThickness, Insulin, and BMI) contained zero values that are not biologically plausible in a living patient \f1\emdash\f0  these were treated as missing data rather than genuine measurements.\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-260\li420\sa100 Missing values: Zero entries in the above five columns were replaced with NaN and imputed using the column median.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Feature scaling: All input features were standardized using StandardScaler (zero mean, unit variance), which is important for distance-based models such as SVM and KNN.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Train-test split: The dataset was split 80% training / 20% testing using stratified sampling to preserve class balance, with a fixed random seed (42) for reproducibility.\par

\pard\sb320\sa160\cf2\b\fs30 5. Models + Methodology\par

\pard\sa160\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\fs22 Five classification algorithms were selected to provide a broad comparison across linear, tree-based, ensemble, margin-based, and instance-based learning approaches:\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-260\li420\sa100 Logistic Regression \f1\emdash\f0  a simple, interpretable linear baseline commonly used in medical prediction tasks.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Decision Tree \f1\emdash\f0  captures non-linear feature interactions and produces an interpretable, rule-based structure (max depth = 5, to reduce overfitting).\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Random Forest \f1\emdash\f0  an ensemble of 200 decision trees, generally more robust and less prone to overfitting than a single tree.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Support Vector Machine (SVM) \f1\emdash\f0  uses an RBF kernel to find an optimal separating margin in a higher-dimensional feature space.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) \f1\emdash\f0  an instance-based learner (k = 9) that classifies based on the majority vote of nearby training samples.\par

\pard\sa160\sl276\slmult1 All models were trained on the same preprocessed and scaled training set, and evaluated on the same held-out test set, ensuring a fair comparison. Training and prediction time were also recorded for each model, since this is relevant to how responsive a live dashboard prediction can be.\par

